  "f72182e1a76b": {
    "text": "01 · The world looks normal",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "1fece119ebb0": {
    "text": "Grain in storage. Fruit on the shelf. Coffee waiting to be brewed.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "a20f46e9a816": {
    "text": "02 · Invisible change · through the lens",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "8b2556c3f80f": {
    "text": "Nothing looks wrong. But chemistry doesn’t wait for us to notice.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "0d7e3c187253": {
    "text": "Food can begin changing before the warning becomes visible. The contours are an illustration of a volatile (VOC) pattern shift, not a measured plume.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "8990d6b3e104": {
    "text": "03–04 · Follow the signal",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "b3dadc07b465": {
    "text": "We can’t see it — but a receptor can sense it.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "b0b8e7869984": {
    "text": "We borrowed part of a fruit fly’s sense of smell: OR + Orco sense an odor cue, Ca²⁺ rises, GCaMP glows — faintly.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "6e02d06d13ee": {
    "text": "05 · Read",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "f4d24057ee21": {
    "text": "So we designed a reader for signals almost hidden in noise: modulated ~470 nm excitation, a photodiode, and digital lock-in processing. The trace is illustrative.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "f45228045eb2": {
    "text": "Current CAD · removable gas lid",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "923b08281e5c": {
    "text": "Click the reader to lift its lid",
    "tag": "span"
  },
  "99fe73d2112b": {
    "text": "06 · Decode",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "baa06a59164f": {
    "text": "One odor. Many receptors. The pattern tells the story.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "2452275c8558": {
    "text": "Illustrative pattern — not measured data.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "f3bb06afa8a3": {
    "text": "07 · Back to the real world",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "c1803e6b0910": {
    "text": "Still looks fine. Inspect sooner.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "fb397bf9551e": {
    "text": "Visual inspection finds nothing obvious; the odor pattern has begun to shift. AeroSense is a screening layer: it suggests follow-up, it does not confirm mold or toxins.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "08a91e09c6a2": {
    "text": "A living sense",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "867dce85dfcf": {
    "text": "Sense what",
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  "7e070e98482b": {
    "text": "you can’t see.",
    "tag": "em"
  },
  "6e95428fa0b1": {
    "text": "A living-cell approach to food-quality screening—with fly receptors, fluorescence, and odor decoding.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "13ce852c6714": {
    "text": "Start with the science",
    "tag": "a"
  },
  "35cd94cec7c7": {
    "text": "AIR → SIGNAL",
    "tag": "span"
  },
  "45cf3bb0f612": {
    "text": "Follow the scent.",
    "tag": "strong"
  },
  "0231dcac37b3": {
    "text": "25 fields · 12 conditions",
    "tag": "strong"
  },
  "a67cfc2b56a0": {
    "text": "Endpoint microscopy · one batch, before G418 selection",
    "tag": "span"
  },
  "fa27962604c6": {
    "text": "4-well reader design",
    "tag": "strong"
  },
  "07443f047404": {
    "text": "Simulation-guided design · physical validation pending",
    "tag": "span"
  },
  "a2cd355d459c": {
    "text": "External-data benchmark",
    "tag": "strong"
  },
  "173d030677c1": {
    "text": "Metal-oxide sensors · not our cell measurements",
    "tag": "span"
  },
  "dc46b29958c7": {
    "text": "01 / The system",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "1c9c9be9f19d": {
    "text": "From sensing",
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  "6e4a7eb18031": {
    "text": "to decisions.",
    "tag": "em"
  },
  "86d14c72d775": {
    "text": "Scroll to turn ↓",
    "tag": "span"
  },
  "79687e225927": {
    "text": "Olfaction · editorial illustration",
    "tag": "span"
  },
  "aecc912e5a8f": {
    "text": "Wet lab",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "82ea31ae7e40": {
    "text": "Let biology",
    "tag": "h3"
  },
  "3e768f54b9c5": {
    "text": "sense.",
    "tag": "em"
  },
  "80cd995d942e": {
    "text": "One batch of 25 image fields across 12 conditions shows reporter expression before selection. Crowded cells and the lack of independent replication limit interpretation.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "1fad7eef9c8e": {
    "text": "Read the results",
    "tag": "a"
  },
  "47a926e846e9": {
    "text": "Reader design · cut-paper study",
    "tag": "span"
  },
  "bb55cf1a908d": {
    "text": "Read the",
    "tag": "h3"
  },
  "0eb225b2ca3b": {
    "text": "faint glow.",
    "tag": "em"
  },
  "0b3d4cdde331": {
    "text": "Optical and gas-transport simulations guide a four-well reader. Fabrication and physical performance tests are still pending.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
  "231f0c280bdd": {
    "text": "Decoding · editorial illustration",
    "tag": "span"
  },
  "558b95675f55": {
    "text": "Find meaning",
    "tag": "h3"
  },
  "7930a1842d2f": {
    "text": "in the pattern.",
    "tag": "em"
  },
  "7f45ba8f2a28": {
    "text": "A fly-inspired decoder was tested on external metal-oxide sensor data. Decoding AeroSense cell signals remains unvalidated.",
    "tag": "p"
  },
